Bundled SVTR network components

Source project: OpenOCR, https://github.com/Topdu/OpenOCR
Source revision: 1ccfc6ee6161f7133b192e16af3a9265273997ba
Source license: Apache License, Version 2.0 (included as LICENSE).
Attribution: the OpenOCR authors and contributors.

Files adapted from that revision:
- layers.py: drop_path, DropPath, Identity and Mlp from openrec/modeling/common.py.
- ctc_blocks.py: ConvBNLayer, ConvMixer, Attention and Block from
  openrec/modeling/encoders/svtrnet.py.
- svtr_encoder.py: openrec/modeling/encoders/svtrv2_lnconv_two33.py.
- ctc_decoder.py: openrec/modeling/decoders/ctc_decoder.py.

Changes made by this project: extract only required components, replace external
imports with package-relative imports, and replace string evaluation of the CTC
normalization class with an explicit LayerNorm check. Network tensor names and
operations used by the trained checkpoints are preserved. network.py provides a
local constructor restricted to the supported encoder and CTC decoder.

The external OpenOCR package, checkout, configuration and vocabulary files are
not required at runtime. This attribution documents code origin; it is not a
claim that the bundled network components were invented by this project.
